menu "BME280 sensor source (Lab 3)"

    config LAB_SIM_BME280
        bool "Use simulated BME280 (bme280_sim) instead of the real I2C driver"
        default y
        help
            When enabled (the default -- required for QEMU, which has no I2C
            BME280 device), this component compiles a synthetic bme280_init()/
            bme280_read() pair: slow-sine temperature (20-25 degC), pressure
            close to 1013 hPa, humidity close to 45%. main/bme280_i2c.c (the
            real driver, hardware only) is compiled OUT in this case.

            When disabled, this component's source file is empty (see its
            "#if CONFIG_LAB_SIM_BME280" guard) and main/bme280_i2c.c's real
            i2c_master driver provides bme280_init()/bme280_read() instead,
            talking to an actual BME280 over I2C.

            Same bme280.h API either way -- app_main() does not change.

endmenu
